From 0b7780121ab5b9f586751d5ff61ef754810e2de3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nil <lue.gsk.2012@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:55:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(qwen4_exp cuda): serve with a draft list file
 (--draft-vocab)

The CUDA engine always drafted over the built-in list, which leaves out most
frequent Japanese tokens. --draft-vocab names a file of upstream token ids
that replaces it; a vocabulary-pruned checkpoint maps a named list through
ple-token-ids.json the same way as the built-in one (draft_rows). A row
count N keeps meaning the rows below N.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011XiGQHTjzpMVa5sTqiQmg5
